# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 12: RECOVERY CONTROLS & FOLLOW-UP RULES

**Route:** `/mctb/setup/recovery`  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-12-RECOVERY-CONTROLS.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–10

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** MCTB Recovery Controls (`/mctb/setup/recovery`, Home pause/resume, legacy `/mctb/setup/business-hours`, `/mctb/setup/follow-up`).

## Architecture correction (LOCKED)

**No Business Hours / weekly schedule page for MCTB.** Carrier conditional forwarding determines when unanswered calls reach Transovo — the business answers or doesn't.

**Replaces:** standalone Business Hours + separate Follow-up Rules nav entries → **one page: Recovery Controls**

## Primary job

1. **Operational:** Active / Pause (presets, 24h, custom date-time, indefinite) / Resume now — shared with Home
2. **Follow-up:** repeat-caller cooldown + max automated recovery messages (runtime-defined period)

## Pause semantics (LOCKED)

| Pause is NOT | |
|--------------|---|
| Carrier forwarding disabled | |
| Customer opt-out | |
| Sender failure | |

Use reason `recovery_paused` — not `recipient_opted_out`. Calls may still log; automated recovery texts stop. No backlog blast on resume.

## Follow-up rules

- Repeat calls = **separate** missed-call events; cooldown suppresses duplicate **texts**
- Cooldown basis = last automated recovery send (backend authoritative)
- Press-1 system confirmation + opener = one recovery attempt if domain defines
- Opt-out/exclusion/sender/consent override follow-up limits
- No drip campaigns, AI bypass, workflow builder

## Wizard

No dedicated wizard step — sensible defaults; optional summary at Test review.

## Text Back alignment

One recovery opener — **no** required business-hours/after-hours message variants (spec 10 corrected).

## Legacy routes

`/mctb/setup/business-hours`, `/mctb/setup/follow-up` → redirect/resolve to `/mctb/setup/recovery`

